 '["LCP measures loading performance; aim for a good experience within 2.5 seconds.","INP measures responsiveness across interactions; aim for an INP below 200 milliseconds.","CLS measures visual stability; aim for a CLS below 0.1.","Core Web Vitals matter, but a perfect score does not guarantee rankings.","Prioritize fixes by user impact and root cause rather than by chasing one lab score.","Performance is a product quality concern spanning design, frontend architecture, and infrastructure."]'::jsonb,
 '[["What are Core Web Vitals?","They are user-centered metrics for loading performance, responsiveness, and visual stability: LCP, INP, and CLS."],["What is a good LCP score?","Google''s good threshold is 2.5 seconds or less at the 75th percentile."],["What is a good INP score?","Google''s good threshold is below 200 milliseconds at the 75th percentile."],["What is a good CLS score?","Google''s good threshold is below 0.1 at the 75th percentile."],["Do Core Web Vitals guarantee rankings?","No. Google states that good Core Web Vitals do not guarantee top rankings."],["Should teams use lab or field data?","Both are useful. Lab data helps diagnose causes; field data shows real user experience."],["What should be optimized first?","Start with the highest-impact user-visible bottleneck on an important page or interaction."]]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb,
 'Core Web Vitals Explained: LCP, INP, CLS & SEO | Kapitech',
 'Learn what LCP, INP, and CLS measure, their current good thresholds, common causes of poor scores, and how to prioritize performance work for SEO and UX.',
 'https://kapitech.id/insights/core-web-vitals/hero.svg',
 'https://kapitech.id/insights/core-web-vitals-explained',
 '{"source":"seo-educational-editorial-pack","research_backed":true,"template":"mvp-vs-prototype-vs-proof-of-concept","structure_version":"103-blocks"}'::jsonb,
 NOW(),
 NOW()
)
